# Central path configuration for this repo's bootstrap scripts.
#
# Each value below can be EITHER:
#   - a RELATIVE fragment (e.g. ".local/downloads") - joined with the
#     current user's home directory ($HOME on Linux, %USERPROFILE% on
#     Windows) at runtime, same on both OSes; or
#   - an ABSOLUTE path (e.g. "D:\tools\download" or "/opt/tools/download")
#     - used exactly as given, never joined with home.
#
# Windows and Linux paths are NEVER interchangeable - a drive letter and
# backslashes mean nothing on Linux, and a leading "/" is just another
# path segment on Windows, not root. So if the bare key below is absolute
# and shaped for one OS, add a "_WINDOWS" or "_LINUX" suffixed key with
# the other OS's value - it takes priority over the bare key on that OS.
# If you run this repo on an OS where the bare key's absolute path doesn't
# make sense and no suffixed override exists, every script that resolves
# these (Get-BootstrapPaths in common.ps1, and prereq.ps1/prereq.sh by
# hand) fails fast with a clear error instead of silently mangling it.
#
# Right now only Windows values are set below (as plain, unsuffixed
# absolute paths) - add DOWNLOADS_DIR_LINUX / INSTALL_DIR_LINUX /
# BACKUP_DIR_LINUX (examples commented out at the bottom) before running
# this repo's Linux path with these same absolute-path values in mind.
#
# Plain KEY=value text on purpose, not YAML/PSD1: this exact file is read
# by THREE different runtimes - bash (bootstrap/prereq.sh), the stock
# Windows PowerShell 5.1 (bootstrap/prereq.ps1), and pwsh7 (everything
# else, via bootstrap/common.ps1's Get-BootstrapPaths). The prereq scripts
# run before pwsh7 exists, so they can't rely on a PowerShell-specific
# config format - this has to parse with grep/cut in bash and a plain
# regex match in PowerShell, nothing fancier.
#
# DOWNLOADS_DIR: where downloaded archives (.zip / .tar.gz / self-extracting
# .exe) are saved before extraction. They are kept afterwards, not deleted -
# so a re-run that finds the same file already here skips re-downloading it,
# and you can always see exactly what got pulled down.
DOWNLOADS_DIR=D:\tools\download

# INSTALL_DIR: where portable tools get extracted to, one subfolder per
# tool (<INSTALL_DIR>/git, <INSTALL_DIR>/wezterm, <INSTALL_DIR>/pwsh7,
# <INSTALL_DIR>/mise, ...). Every install script resolves its executable
# from inside its own subfolder here and adds that subfolder to PATH -
# nothing gets copied out into a separate bin directory.
INSTALL_DIR=D:\tools\apps

# BACKUP_DIR: before Sync-DotLink (bootstrap/common.ps1) copies this repo's
# tracked version of a config file over an existing real file/folder (e.g.
# you already had a ~/.gitconfig or ~/.config/nvim before ever running this
# repo), it moves whatever was already there into
# <BACKUP_DIR>/<timestamp>/<same relative path under home> first, so
# nothing is ever silently lost - then copies the repo's version on top.
# Only used by bootstrap.ps1/common.ps1 (pwsh7) - the prereq scripts never
# touch dotfile deployment, only pwsh7 itself.
BACKUP_DIR=D:\tools\backup

# Linux overrides - uncomment and set to real paths before running this
# repo's Linux path, since the bare keys above are Windows-only absolute
# paths and would fail fast with a clear error on Linux otherwise.
DOWNLOADS_DIR_LINUX=/mnt/dev-disk/work/aravello/tools/download
INSTALL_DIR_LINUX=/mnt/dev-disk/work/aravello/tools/apps
BACKUP_DIR_LINUX=/mnt/dev-disk/work/aravello/tools/backup
